 sign: K(r) - K(far) > 0 at all listed r -> cross term +2 lam M1 M2 K raises the weight of nearby
       like masses -> attractive, V(r) = -2 lam M1 M2/(4 pi r) + const, G_N = lam/(2 pi) [lam = kappa^2/4]
 light probe on the lattice: q_1 = 0 for a source uniform along x, theta_11(q_1=0) = 1 exactly ->
       (rho_l + A_l)/rho_l = 2 exactly -> 1 + gamma = 2;  Newton-only bridge (no rho A term): ratio 1, gamma = 0

